    "type": 0,
    "content": "# TOOLS: \n- Copy Paste your Tome data and compare yourself to the top 10 or other high end players with:\n➡️  <https://cephyric-gh.github.io/tome/>\n- You can also use \"Trialpear's Crappy Tome Sheet\" as here you could highlight or write notes of stuff you are focusing on\n➡️ <https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/u/0/d/1x3YNRUwN7Fw-ewzQC58rop-hkObvy20FHSY1IKXkCM0>\n\n\n**Rewards:**\n- You can claim monthly nametags up to the % you reach and hand them in at w7 Gallery (Codfrey) for permanent passive rewards\n- Nametag claim resets on the 17th-18th (depending on time zone), see <https://idleontoolbox.com/account/world-4/tome>\n- - The 0.1% = ||20% DR Multi + AFK Multi|| The 0.5% = || 17% Bonus kills + all Stats|| The 1% = || 15% Class Xp Multi + Bonus Money|| The 5% = ||12% Dmg +  MK/tier Multi|| The 10% = || 10% Total Dmg + Mob Respawn|| The 25% = ||7% Fight and Skill AFK gain|| The 50% = ||5% DR and Money||\n**Tip:**\n- **Best method for 0.1% is to instantly check and go for it after an update!**\n- Tome Points update every day now (used to only be when Lava pushed it), so it may increase just a few pts or even 100+ pts in a day if a ton of people push for 0.1%.\n- Focus on some of the permanent Tome Points, stuff that doesn't keep scaling like samples but rather \"Fastest cEfaunt kill\" (1 sec) and then focus on other tome pts that are easy to Max/Cap, followed by things that keep scaling like Sample size etc.\n- This list is just some stuff you could highlight in the above sheet to track easier, like i wrote an X in column A so I could easily find what i had to do, then removed it once i did it. By no means is this perfect, but it does show you the things that shouldnt be too hard to get going if you are in W7 and have played a bit.",
